How Data Is Stored in the Cloud & How the Operator Accesses It
1. Where Does the Data Store When Re-Connecting to the Internet?
The system uses a two-tier offline-first cloud architecture specifically engineered for rural areas in Sindh with intermittent 2G/3G/4G connectivity:
code
Code
[ Head Teacher's Mobile Phone in Field ]
     │
     ├── 1. While Offline:
     │      • Text Data & Rolls → IndexedDB / Local Storage queue
     │      • Form-B / CNIC / Profile Photos → Compressed local blob cache
     │
     ├── 2. When Reconnected to Internet (4G/WiFi) or on "Sync Now":
     │      │
     │      ├── A. Textual & Structured Records
     │      │      └── Pushed via /api/cloud/sync to SEF Central Cloud Database
     │      │          (cloud_storage/sef_central_cloud_db.json)
     │      │          • GR Numbers, Student & Staff Bio-data
     │      │          • Class Roll Call & Staff Attendance
     │      │          • Examination Marks & Gazette
     │      │          • Issues, Tasks & Expense Records
     │      │
     │      └── B. Scans & Image Documents (Form-B, CNIC, Photos)
     │             └── Uploaded to Central Cloud Object Storage Vault
     │                 (cloud_storage/documents_and_photos/)
     │                 • Student Profile Photos
     │                 • Scanned NADRA Form-B Copies
     │                 • Father & Mother CNIC Front/Back Copies
     │                 • Teacher & Peon CNIC & Appointment Letters
     │                 • Each file gets a secure URL linked to that record
     │
     ▼
[ SEF Central Cloud Server & Audit Ledger ]
     ▲
     │
[ Operator Dashboard on Mobile Phone / Tablet / PC ]
